    "pressure": {
      "file": "oil_seal_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Narrow, controlled lip contact",
      "description": "The lip is moulded slightly smaller than the shaft (interference) and the garter spring adds radial load, so it contacts the shaft over a band only ≈ 0.1–0.3 mm wide. A thin oil film under the lip lubricates it; the asymmetric lip angles (steeper on the oil side) create a pumping action that returns oil. Lip seals suit low pressure (≈ ≤ 0.5 bar) and surface speeds up to about 10–30 m/s depending on the elastomer; the dust lip keeps dirt out.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
  },
